  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "17862072",
      "title": "The \"angular.json\" File - A Closer Look",
      "lectureOrder": 739,
      "videoOrder": 679,
      "sourceHash": "a7ea2195d52443e57046a3809fc088e0d868b859b0c7e9af26afb9d00e9887f8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "Instructor: So what's inside of the angular json file?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 7.44,
          "en": "This is a file which is generated automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.44,
          "end": 9.6,
          "en": "when you generate a new angler project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.6,
          "end": 11.79,
          "en": "And this is used by the cli",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.79,
          "end": 15.96,
          "en": "behind the scenes to run different cli commands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.96,
          "end": 18.15,
          "en": "and to know how to run these commands.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.15,
          "end": 21.3,
          "en": "Basically here you can set some defaults",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.3,
          "end": 22.74,
          "en": "for all these flags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.74,
          "end": 25.62,
          "en": "You could otherwise add manually to every command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 28.2,
          "en": "And of course setting defaults is more appropriate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.2,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "because it saves you the hassle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 32.43,
          "en": "of having to add all these flags all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.43,
          "end": 34.35,
          "en": "So what do we have in there?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.35,
          "end": 36.45,
          "en": "Now this angular json file uses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.45,
          "end": 40.56,
          "en": "well, the json data format to, well, store its information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.56,
          "end": 43.26,
          "en": "and there it follows a certain schema, which is developed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 46.32,
          "en": "by the angler team and it's stored in this folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.32,
          "end": 49.53,
          "en": "Not something we should change, just some information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.53,
          "end": 51.72,
          "en": "The version here, you can leave this the way it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.72,
          "end": 56.49,
          "en": "This is just the version of this file format here basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.49,
          "end": 59.94,
          "en": "Interesting, is the new project route entry here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.94,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "This controls where new projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 65.73,
          "en": "in your, project here, in the end are added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.73,
          "end": 67.08,
          "en": "This might not tell you much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.08,
          "end": 68.52,
          "en": "What are projects?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.52,
          "end": 69.87,
          "en": "We'll come back to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.87,
          "end": 71.55,
          "en": "It turns out that you can manage more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.55,
          "end": 75.45,
          "en": "than one project in a angular project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.45,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "And thus far, from the entire course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 79.47,
          "en": "we always had just one project, one app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.47,
          "end": 80.7,
          "en": "While you can manage more,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 80.7,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "I will show you how later in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 85.14,
          "en": "For now, let's go with that one project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 85.14,
          "end": 87.27,
          "en": "So next we have this project entry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 87.27,
          "end": 91.2,
          "en": "And there you have one nested entry per project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 91.2,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "Now as I mentioned, we have one project here and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "if I make this smaller, we see there only is one entry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 100.89,
          "en": "And that also, you see, is the default project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 100.89,
          "end": 103.97999999999999,
          "en": "against which our seal I commands will run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.97999999999999,
          "end": 105.84,
          "en": "If you add multiple projects, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 105.84,
          "end": 107.34,
          "en": "something I will show you later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 107.34,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "Then you could specify here which project the seal commands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "like generate and on will run against.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 115.11,
          "en": "But here we only have one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 115.11,
          "end": 117.09,
          "en": "So let's expand this again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 117.09,
          "end": 118.92,
          "en": "Now we see which project type does this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 118.92,
          "end": 120.51,
          "en": "and here it's an application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 120.51,
          "end": 122.34,
          "en": "Now, you have multiple types here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 122.34,
          "end": 124.35,
          "en": "You have application and library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 124.35,
          "end": 126.42,
          "en": "And by the way, you get all the completion here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 126.42,
          "end": 129.57,
          "en": "Either automatically or by hitting controlled space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 129.57,
          "end": 131.01,
          "en": "The default is application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 131.01,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "which is a regular angler web application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 135.51,
          "en": "but you could change this to library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 135.51,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "and I will show you what a library is later in this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 141.18,
          "en": "For now, let's leave it at application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 141.18,
          "end": 142.62,
          "en": "Then we get the schematics here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 142.62,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "Schematics doesn't tell us much, but schematics actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 149.64,
          "en": "is a really cool feature of the angular ecosystem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 149.64,
          "end": 150.51,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 150.51,
          "end": 152.43,
          "en": "And we'll come back to what schematics are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 152.43,
          "end": 154.2,
          "en": "for now, let's ignore it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 154.2,
          "end": 158.37,
          "en": "Route basically tells the angular cli what the route folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 158.37,
          "end": 159.81,
          "en": "of this project is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 159.81,
          "end": 163.05,
          "en": "And here it's the, well, folder here itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 163.05,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "so the entire folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 166.71,
          "en": "And then where our source files live in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 166.71,
          "end": 170.7,
          "en": "And you could change this if you wanna store your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 170.7,
          "end": 172.26,
          "en": "in a different folder than source,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 172.26,
          "end": 174.18,
          "en": "but I'll of course leave it at source",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 174.18,
          "end": 175.77,
          "en": "but you can change this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 175.77,
          "end": 177.6,
          "en": "Here you set the default prefix,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 177.6,
          "end": 179.73,
          "en": "which is added in front of every component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 179.73,
          "end": 181.02,
          "en": "So if you don't wanna use app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 181.02,
          "end": 183.15,
          "en": "you can use a different one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 183.15,
          "end": 186,
          "en": "And then you get this architect command here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 186,
          "end": 187.77,
          "en": "this architect area, which is the rest",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 187.77,
          "end": 189.364,
          "en": "of our project specific settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 189.364,
          "end": 192.347,
          "en": "Now, here, the different commands you can execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 192.347,
          "end": 194.67,
          "en": "can be configured.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 194.67,
          "end": 197.13,
          "en": "For example, the build command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 197.13,
          "end": 200.55,
          "en": "There you see which tool gets used under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 200.55,
          "end": 201.96,
          "en": "And this is a tool which is part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 201.96,
          "end": 204.03,
          "en": "of the angular devkit package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 204.03,
          "end": 209.03,
          "en": "which is one of the third party dependencies we have added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 211.02,
          "end": 214.95,
          "en": "And this basically is just the the tool, the configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 214.95,
          "end": 218.4,
          "en": "the code, which knows how to build an angular project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 218.4,
          "end": 221.16,
          "en": "So which steps to execute and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 221.16,
          "end": 224.97,
          "en": "And this tool can be configured with options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 224.97,
          "end": 227.64,
          "en": "These are options you also, at least partly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 227.64,
          "end": 231.18,
          "en": "can set with these extra configuration flags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 231.18,
          "end": 232.41,
          "en": "on cli commands.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 232.41,
          "end": 235.89,
          "en": "So on ng build dash dash aot for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 235.89,
          "end": 237.9,
          "en": "controls that this should be built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 237.9,
          "end": 241.38,
          "en": "with ahead of time compilation and by default this is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 241.38,
          "end": 242.64,
          "en": "So you would only need to set this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 242.64,
          "end": 244.35,
          "en": "if you want to set it to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 244.35,
          "end": 246.78,
          "en": "But you can set this with a flag or,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 246.78,
          "end": 248.67,
          "en": "if you know this should always be the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 248.67,
          "end": 251.67,
          "en": "Here, for example, with that aot option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 251.67,
          "end": 253.56,
          "en": "There you see the default is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 253.56,
          "end": 258,
          "en": "but if I set this to false, now all builds would be done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 258,
          "end": 261.543,
          "en": "with the aot compilation turned off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 262.89,
          "end": 265.92,
          "en": "We see where the project should be output into.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 265.92,
          "end": 267.78,
          "en": "And here we see that is the dist folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 267.78,
          "end": 270.63,
          "en": "and then the angular config sub folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 270.63,
          "end": 272.61,
          "en": "We see what our route entry file is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 272.61,
          "end": 274.2,
          "en": "And you could change this of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 274.2,
          "end": 277.40999999999997,
          "en": "What the route entry file for the angular application is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 277.40999999999997,
          "end": 279.48,
          "en": "And you could change this as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 279.48,
          "end": 281.73,
          "en": "Where the polyfills are managed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 281.73,
          "end": 282.69,
          "en": "You can change this as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 282.69,
          "end": 284.01,
          "en": "You can change everything here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 284.01,
          "end": 287.76,
          "en": "And what your project specific configuration fault",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 287.76,
          "end": 289.54,
          "en": "Here is configuration file is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 289.54,
          "end": 291.84000000000003,
          "en": "Assets allows you to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 291.84000000000003,
          "end": 296.07,
          "en": "configure which files or folders should be copied over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 296.07,
          "end": 297.18,
          "en": "in the output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 297.18,
          "end": 299.43,
          "en": "In the source folder we have an assets folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 299.43,
          "end": 301.17,
          "en": "and there I have nothing in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 301.17,
          "end": 303.6,
          "en": "But if I would store let's say an image in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 303.6,
          "end": 307.44,
          "en": "which I always want to be able to use in my application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 307.44,
          "end": 308.7,
          "en": "I could store it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 308.7,
          "end": 311.55,
          "en": "Reference it from inside my components, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 311.55,
          "end": 313.59,
          "en": "by rendering an image tag there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 313.59,
          "end": 316.53,
          "en": "and it would be copied over into the dist folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 316.53,
          "end": 319.98,
          "en": "so that it is available in the served app as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 319.98,
          "end": 323.439,
          "en": "The styles note is one we used throughout this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 323.439,
          "end": 324.963,
          "en": "project to include bootstrap.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 324.963,
          "end": 327.72,
          "en": "Here you can set up which css files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 327.72,
          "end": 330.84,
          "en": "either your own ones or third party package files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 330.84,
          "end": 334.14,
          "en": "should be included in the application by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 334.14,
          "end": 336.69,
          "en": "Of course every component has its own style file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 337.523,
          "en": "as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 337.523,
          "end": 340.23,
